                        "review": "**Near Death – A Brutal but Brilliant Survival Experience**\r\n\r\n**9/10 – Highly Recommended**\r\n\r\nI started playing Near Death on Normal difficulty and absolutely loved it. The game was already challenging, but I enjoyed the atmosphere, the survival mechanics, and the constant pressure of trying to stay alive in such a hostile environment.\r\n\r\nThen I decided to try the hardest difficulty, Condition 1. And let me tell you, that was a completely different experience!\r\n\r\nDon't get me wrong, Normal difficulty is still challenging, but Condition 1 is absolutely brutal. This is not a game where you can simply run around and hope for the best. You need to pay attention to everything: your direction, the order of your objectives, your supplies, and your timing.\r\n\r\nEvery decision matters. Make one wrong move, miss an important objective, or waste precious supplies, and you could find yourself having to start over from the beginning. Unless you've managed to secure a good saving position, one mistake can cost you a lot of progress.\r\n\r\nWhat makes Near Death so good is that it forces you to think carefully and plan ahead. You're not just fighting against the environment; you're constantly fighting against your own mistakes. The tension and satisfaction of finally overcoming a difficult section make the experience incredibly rewarding.\r\n\r\nHonestly, this is one of the best single-player survival games I've played. It manages to make survival feel genuinely challenging without relying on the usual combat-heavy mechanics.\r\n\r\nIf you enjoy survival games that test your patience, planning, and ability to adapt, I highly recommend giving Near Death a try.\r\n\r\n**9/10 – A fantastic survival game that will keep you on your toes, especially if you're brave enough to attempt Condition 1!**",
